  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;be a set of all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> -digit natural numbers whose exactly one digit is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math>.&nbsp;Then the probability that a randomly chosen element of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> leaves remainder <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> when divided by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> is:"
  },
